    spellResistance: "Yes",
    summary: "This power enables you to warp the consciousness and senses of one or more creatures, sending the victim into a catatonic state. Power Points: 17. Augment: For every additional power point you spend, the number of individual and group hit points the power can affect increases 10. For example, if you spend 2 ditional points, the single target sion of the power affects a creature that currently has 120 or fewer points, and the area effect version is usable against creatures each currently have 50 or fewer points, up to a total of 320 hit points of such creatures.",
    description: "This power enables you to warp the consciousness and senses of one or more creatures, sending the victim into a catatonic state. When microcosm is manifested, you can target either a single creature within range or a group of creatures all located within the power’s area. Single Target: If microcosm targets a single creature, that creature’s senses are pinched off from the real world if it currently has 100 or fewer hit points. The subject’s senses are all completely fabricated from within own mind, though it may not realize this. In reality, the subject sprawls limply, drooling and mewling, eventually dies of thirst and starvation without care. The subject within its own made-up world until the time of its actual death. Area Effect: If microcosm is manifested on an area, it sends all affected creatures into a shared catatonia world is a construct, but within world, the victims can interact each other). It affects only creatures that currently have 30 or fewer points, and only up to a total of 300 points of such creatures. The power affects creatures with the lowest point totals first. (Creatures negative hit points count as having hit points.) Manifesting microcosm a second time on an affected creature turns its sensory pathways outward once more. Otherwise, only very potent powers (such as psychic chirurgery or reality revision) or similar effects (such as miracle or wish) can undo mental crosswiring that this power brings about. Augment: For every additional power point you spend, the number of individual and group hit points the power can affect increases 10. For example, if you spend 2 ditional points, the single target sion of the power affects a creature that currently has 120 or fewer points, and the area effect version is usable against creatures each currently have 50 or fewer points, up to a total of 320 hit points of such creatures.",
